o-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"present-a-scene-to-a-room\">Present a scene to a room<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#present-a-scene-to-a-room\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Walk clients through a flat, a showroom or a product together: everyone\nopens the same room link, you take the floor, their cameras follow yours,\nyour voice reaches them from where your avatar stands, and every tour\nstep, hotspot, material variant, light change and section cut you make\nappears on their screens as you make it.</p>\n<p><strong>You need:</strong> a scene link (any share link works, public or private) and\na room name. No account; the room name is the only secret, so pick one\nnobody will guess (<code>showflat-42-tue-3pm</code>, not <code>demo</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-open-the-room\">1. Open the room<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#1-open-the-room\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Add <code>?room=&lt;name&gt;</code> to the scene link and send it round. Each viewer can\nadd <code>&amp;as=&lt;their name&gt;</code>; otherwise they appear as &quot;guest&quot;. The **viewers\npanel** (bottom right) lists everyone in the room with a coloured dot —\nthe same colour as their in-world avatar.</p>\n<p>Up to 32 viewers share a room. Everyone sees everyone&#39;s avatar move live.</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-talk\">2. Talk<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#2-talk\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Click <strong>Join voice</strong>. The browser asks for the microphone once. From then\non:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Mute / Unmute</strong> your own microphone.</li><li><strong>Open mic</strong> ↔ <strong>Push-to-talk</strong>: with push-to-talk, hold <strong>T</strong> (or the\n<em>Hold to talk</em> button) while you speak.</li><li><strong>Spatial</strong> ↔ <strong>Stereo</strong>: by default each voice comes from where that\nperson&#39;s avatar stands and fades with distance (useful in a large\nflat); Stereo plays everyone flat and at full level.</li><li><strong>Mute</strong> next to a name silences that one person for you only.</li></ul>\n<p>The dot next to a name pulses while they speak, and their avatar\nbrightens in the scene. &quot;muted&quot; next to a name means they muted\nthemselves.</p>\n<p>Voice is peer-to-peer between the browsers: nothing is recorded and no\naudio passes through the Verse server (only the connection handshake\ndoes). Two limits follow from that:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Six talkers per room.</strong> A seventh person who joins voice sees &quot;Voice\nis limited to 6 talkers&quot; and hears nothing; viewers who do not join\nvoice are not counted. For larger audiences, present with voice among\nthe six and let the rest watch.</li><li><strong>Direct connections first, a relay when the server has one.</strong> Most home\nand office networks connect directly. Phones on mobile data (carrier\nNAT) and strict corporate firewalls often cannot; voice then goes\nthrough a TURN relay if the server has one configured (see\n<a href=\"/docs/guides/tour-together#voice\" id=\"lnk-tour-together-voice\">Tour together § Voice</a>). Without a relay, a\npair that cannot connect sees &quot;No audio with &lt;name&gt; — the network blocks\na direct connection&quot;; a phone hotspot or a different network on one side\nfixes\nit. Everything else in the room keeps working.</li></ul>\n<p>Add <code>&amp;voice=1</code> (open mic) or <code>&amp;voice=ptt</code> to the link to join voice as\nthe page opens.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-present\">3. Present<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#3-present\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Click <strong>Present</strong> in the viewers panel (or open the link with\n<code>&amp;present=1</code>). For everyone else:</p>\n<ul><li>their camera glides to yours and stays with it — you walk, they walk;</li><li>a veil over their viewport says <em>Following &lt;you&gt;</em> with two buttons:\n<strong>Take control</strong> (their own camera again; a <em>Rejoin the presenter</em> chip\nbrings them back) and <strong>Raise hand</strong>;</li><li>your <strong>Play tour</strong>, hotspot jumps, <strong>Variant</strong>, <strong>Lights</strong> and\n<strong>Section</strong> changes happen on their screens too;</li><li>the point under your pointer is drawn for them as a red laser dot.</li></ul>\n<p>A raised hand pulses that person&#39;s row in your panel for a few seconds.\n<strong>Hand over</strong> next to a name makes them the presenter (you start\nfollowing them); <strong>Stop presenting</strong> gives everyone their camera back.\nIf someone else clicks Present while you are presenting, they take over\n— the panel tells you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-in-an-embed\">4. In an embed<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#4-in-an-embed\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The same room works inside your own page through the embed SDK:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const viewer = Verse.embed(el, { model: &quot;ingest/&lt;id&gt;.vpk&quot; });\nviewer.joinRoom(&quot;showflat-42&quot;, { name: &quot;Alex&quot;, voice: true });\nviewer.present(true);                       // take the floor\nviewer.on(&quot;speaking&quot;, (s) =&gt; roster.mark(s.id, s.speaking));\nviewer.on(&quot;peer&quot;, (p) =&gt; p.state === &quot;hand&quot; &amp;&amp; toast(`${p.name} raised a hand`));\nviewer.on(&quot;room&quot;, (r) =&gt; r.state === &quot;notice&quot; &amp;&amp; toast(r.message));</code></pre></div>\n<p>The follower veil, laser dot and the presenter&#39;s actions all render\ninside the frame; <code>setVoice({ muted, pushToTalk, talking, spatial })</code>\ndrives the voice knobs from your own controls. Reference:\n<a href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-md\">embed-sdk.md</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"good-to-know\">Good to know<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#good-to-know\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li>Rooms are memory-only on the server: a restart empties them and\neveryone&#39;s page reconnects by itself.</li><li>Voice needs HTTPS (or <code>localhost</code>) — browsers do not expose the\nmicrophone on plain HTTP.</li><li>Voice uses the WebRTC and Web Audio panner APIs every current browser\nships; the automated gate exercises Chromium, so treat Safari and\nFirefox as &quot;should work, not yet proven&quot;.</li><li>Headsets (WebXR) show the avatars and hear the voices; presenting from\ninside a headset is not offered.</li></ul></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#1-open-the-room\" id=\"lnk-1-open-the-room\">1. Open the room</a><a href=\"#2-talk\" id=\"lnk-2-talk\">2. Talk</a><a href=\"#3-present\" id=\"lnk-3-present\">3. Present</a><a href=\"#4-in-an-embed\" id=\"lnk-4-in-an-embed\">4. In an embed</a><a href=\"#good-to-know\" id=\"lnk-good-to-know\">Good to know</a></aside></section>"}